{
  "dom_id": "step-e5361",
  "name": "Example: Finding the X-Intercepts of a Hyperbola",
  "problem": "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{10} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{10} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
